# Implementation Plan: Configurable Motion Detection Sensitivity & Segment Padding

## Goal
Expose motion detection parameters (threshold, min contour area, motion frames, buffer sizes, preprocessing) from the UI → pass through to Python scripts → enable dynamic adjustment of video processing sensitivity.

## Plan

### 1. `src/app/page.tsx` - Add UI controls for detection parameters
- Add sliders/inputs for: Sensitivity threshold, Min contour area, Min motion frames, Pre-roll buffer, Post-roll buffer
- Pass parameters to API via query string when submitting upload
- Display parameter values in log panel

### 2. `src/app/api/upload/route.ts` - Accept and forward parameters
- Extract parameters from form data / query string
- Pass them to `process_video.py` as command-line arguments
- Maintain backward compatibility (default values when no params provided)

### 3. `scripts/process_video.py` - Add CLI parameter support
- Add `argparse` for: `--threshold`, `--min-contour`, `--min-motion-frames`, `--buffer-frames`, `--history`, `--var-threshold`
- Map UI values to Python variables:
  - `motion_threshold` ← sensitivity slider (0.001 to 0.05)
  - `min_contour_area` ← minimum blob size (10 to 200)
  - `min_motion_frames` ← sustained motion frames (5 to 30)
  - `buffer_frames` ← pre/post-roll padding in frames (30 to 300)
  - `history` ← MOG2 history length (100 to 500)
  - `var_threshold` ← MOG2 variance threshold (10 to 50)
- Update the progress JSON output to include detected parameters

### 4. `src/lib/worker.ts` - Forward parameters for "process latest"
- Add `processLatestWithParams(params)` function
- Pass parameters to the Python script invocation
- Include params in progress metadata for UI display

### 5. UI feedback
- Show current parameter values in the log panel
- Update as user adjusts sliders

## Files to Modify

- `src/app/page.tsx` - Add parameter state and UI controls
- `src/app/api/upload/route.ts` - Accept and forward CLI params
- `scripts/process_video.py` - Replace hard-coded tunables with argparse
- `src/lib/worker.ts` - Add params-forwarding function

## Architecture

```
UI (page.tsx) ←→ API route ←→ Python process_video.py ←→ Motion detection ←→ Segments
     ↑                                                                        ↓
  Parameter panel                                                          FFmpeg cutting
```

## Backward Compatibility
- All Python parameters have default values matching current hard-coded values
- If no parameters sent, system behaves exactly as before
- Query string params optional; FormData params optional

